  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "spl_fixedarray_object_get_properties",
    "file": "php-src/ext/spl/spl_fixedarray.c",
    "description": "The copy-on-write path at lines 243-246 duplicates a shared object-properties HashTable into `intern->std.properties`, but fails to update the local `ht` pointer to that duplicate. The following element insertion, packed-to-mixed conversion, and return therefore operate on the old shared table, while the SplFixedArray object retains the duplicate in an inappropriate/stale state. With the large rebuild in this PoV, updates repeatedly reallocate packed hash storage; the inconsistent property-table ownership/state is later traversed by `gc_mark_grey()`, which trusts `nNumUsed`/layout and reads beyond the allocation at `zval_get_type()`. The patch-relevant fix is to continue rebuilding and return the duplicated `intern->std.properties` table (for example, assign it back to `ht`) after COW.",
    "conditions": "PHP input creates a non-empty SplFixedArray whose `should_rebuild_properties` flag is set, keeps multiple aliases (`$a`, `$b`, `$c`) so the relevant object/property state survives and becomes shared/GC-visible, and requests debug properties with `var_dump()`. The properties HashTable must have refcount greater than one so the COW branch executes. A large size such as octal `010001000` causes the indexed-property rebuild to grow/reallocate packed hash storage many times. At request shutdown, `zend_gc_collect_cycles()` obtains the object's properties through `spl_fixedarray_object_get_gc()` and traverses the inconsistent table, triggering the heap out-of-bounds read."
  },
